# A library must not pin its own resolution.
Manifest.toml
/Manifest.toml
docs/Manifest.toml
test/Manifest.toml

# The one exception: the repeatability package pins deliberately, because
# reproducing a result on someone else's machine is its entire purpose.
!repeatability/Manifest.toml

docs/build
docs/src/generated

*.mem
.DS_Store
.vscode/settings.json

# --- Large binaries and experiment output -------------------------------
# A blob committed once lives in the history of every clone forever, even if a
# later commit deletes it -- the usual way a research repository ends up with a
# gigabyte-scale clone. The blob-size-guard workflow rejects the rest in CI.
*.jld
*.jld2
*.bson
*.mp4
*.mov
*.avi
*.mkv
*.bundle
outputs/
bench/results/

# Claude Code: track shared commands, ignore personal/local config
.claude/*
!.claude/commands/

# The working plan. Deliberately untracked: it carries candid assessments of
# neighbouring projects and of how to approach their maintainers, which has no
# business in a repository that will be made public. What belongs to everyone
# goes in docs/ or CLAUDE.md instead.
/plan.md
